-- title:
--   Scalar transport: elements projecting to integers act by multiplication
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime. Let $i$ be an element of the abstract Hecke algebra `HeckeAlg`, that is, of the polynomial ring $\mathbb{Z}[X_\ell : \ell \text{ prime}]$ on one variable for each prime, and let $c$ be an integer. Assume that $i$ is carried by the ring homomorphism `heckeProj`, which sends the variable at a prime $\ell$ to $U_\ell$ when $\ell \mid p$ and to $T_\ell$ otherwise, to the image of $c$ under the structure map of $\mathbb{Z}$ into [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra p 2 ∅`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18), the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{C}}$ of weight-two cusp forms for $\Gamma_0(p)$ generated by all the operators $T_\ell$ ($\ell \nmid p$) and $U_q$ ($q \mid p$), no prime being excluded since $S = \emptyset$. Then for every $x$ in `JZero p`, the degree-zero divisor class group $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the modular function field of level $p$ base-changed to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, one has $i \cdot x = c \cdot x$, where the action of $i$ is the `HeckeAlg`-module structure `heckeModuleBar p` (given, the geometric Hecke correspondences on the base-changed curve commuting, by sending the variable at $\ell$ to `heckeOperatorBar p ℓ`), and $c \cdot x$ is the integer scalar multiple in the abelian group `JZero p`.
--
--   This is the scalar-transport step in the comparison of the Hecke action on forms with the Hecke action on the Jacobian $J_0(p)$: an element of the abstract Hecke algebra whose image in the weight-two Hecke algebra of level $p$ is an integer acts on $J_0(p)$ as that integer. It is used in the computation of the index of the Eisenstein ideal, via [`ModularCurve.exists_mem_eisensteinIdeal_smul_eq_eisensteinNumerator_zsmul`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_mem_eisensteinIdeal_smul_eq_eisensteinNumerator_zsmul).
